                            },
                            "claim": "`page()` returns one extra item per page, duplicating the boundary item across pages `end = offset + page_size + 1` widens the slice by one beyond `page_size`; for `page(items, 1, 2)` on `[a,b,c,d]`, `offset=0`, `end=3`, returning `[a,b,c]` (3 items for a page size of 2), and `page(items, 2, 2)` returns `items[2:5]` = `[c,d]`, so `c` appears on both page 1 and page 2. Every page returned by this function contains `page_size + 1` items instead of `page_size`, and the last item of page N is duplicated as the first item of page N+1. Any caller relying on `page_size` as a hard cap (UI page rendering, API pagination contracts, batch-processing chunk sizes) will over-return data and reprocess/redisplay duplicate records.",
                            "extra": {
                                "defect_kind": "off-by-one"
                            }
                        }
