                                    "start": 5,
                                    "end": 6
                                }
                            },
                            "claim": "`make_archive` builds a shell command from unsanitized `name` with `shell=True` `cmd = f\"tar -czf {name}.tar.gz data/\"` interpolates the caller-supplied `name` directly into a shell command string, then executes it via `subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, check=True)`. Any shell metacharacter in `name` (e.g. `` `; rm -rf /` ``, `$(...)`, backticks, `&&`, `|`) is interpreted by the shell rather than treated as a literal filename fragment. The prior implementation passed `[\"tar\", \"-czf\", name + \".tar.gz\", \"data/\"]` as an argument list with `shell=False` (the default), which does not invoke a shell and treats `name` as an opaque argument. If `name` is ever influenced by an external actor (a filename, request parameter, config value, or any caller-controlled string reaching this function), an attacker can execute arbitrary shell commands with the privileges of the process running the backup \u2014 full remote code execution, not merely a malformed archive name.",
                            "extra": {
                                "defect_kind": "command-injection"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
